  "Four rules": "",
  "Never more than three things side by side: the rails, the content, and at most one full column next to it.": "",
  "A rail is the same column, folded. The panel icon at its top opens it, and the open column folds with the same icon. Hovering a rail shows the full column over the content without moving the layout.": "",
  "Any action panel folds the conversation list. The X at the top right of a panel closes it and returns you to reading; the X at the end of the subject bar closes the conversation and returns you to browsing.": "",
  "The work package lives in its own panel on the right, headed Work package. A linked conversation opens with it; the chip in the subject bar folds it and opens it again.": ""
